# This .gitignore file should be placed at the root of your Unity project directory
#
# Get latest from https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Unity.gitignore
#
.utmp/
/[Ll]ibrary/
/[Tt]emp/
/[Oo]bj/
/[Bb]uild/
/[Bb]uilds/
/[Ll]ogs/
/[Uu]ser[Ss]ettings/
*.log

# By default unity supports Blender asset imports, *.blend1 blender files do not need to be committed to version control.
*.blend1
*.blend1.meta

# MemoryCaptures can get excessive in size.
# They also could contain extremely sensitive data
/[Mm]emoryCaptures/

# Recordings can get excessive in size
/[Rr]ecordings/

# Uncomment this line if you wish to ignore the asset store tools plugin
# /[Aa]ssets/AssetStoreTools*

# Autogenerated Jetbrains Rider plugin
/[Aa]ssets/Plugins/Editor/JetBrains*
# Jetbrains Rider personal-layer settings
*.DotSettings.user

# Visual Studio cache directory
.vs/

# Gradle cache directory
.gradle/

# Autogenerated VS/MD/Consulo solution and project files
ExportedObj/
.consulo/
*.csproj
*.unityproj
*.sln
*.suo
*.tmp
*.user
*.userprefs
*.pidb
*.booproj
*.svd
*.pdb
*.mdb
*.opendb
*.VC.db

# Unity3D generated meta files
*.pidb.meta
*.pdb.meta
*.mdb.meta

# Unity3D generated file on crash reports
sysinfo.txt

# Mono auto generated files
mono_crash.*

# Builds
*.apk
*.aab
*.unitypackage
*.unitypackage.meta
*.app

# Crashlytics generated file
crashlytics-build.properties

# TestRunner generated files
InitTestScene*.unity*

# Addressables default ignores, before user customizations
/ServerData
/[Aa]ssets/StreamingAssets/aa*
/[Aa]ssets/AddressableAssetsData/link.xml*
/[Aa]ssets/Addressables_Temp*
# By default, Addressables content builds will generate addressables_content_state.bin
# files in platform-specific subfolders, for example:
# /Assets/AddressableAssetsData/OSX/addressables_content_state.bin
/[Aa]ssets/AddressableAssetsData/*/*.bin*

# Visual Scripting auto-generated files
/[Aa]ssets/Unity.VisualScripting.Generated/VisualScripting.Flow/UnitOptions.db
/[Aa]ssets/Unity.VisualScripting.Generated/VisualScripting.Flow/UnitOptions.db.meta
/[Aa]ssets/Unity.VisualScripting.Generated/VisualScripting.Core/Property Providers
/[Aa]ssets/Unity.VisualScripting.Generated/VisualScripting.Core/Property Providers.meta

# Auto-generated scenes by play mode tests
/[Aa]ssets/[Ii]nit[Tt]est[Ss]cene*.unity*
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local additions below this line are not present in the upstream Unity
# template linked in the header above.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Local addition: XML solution format used by Visual Studio 2022 and later.
# The upstream template ignores *.sln but predates *.slnx.
*.slnx

# Local addition: AI development tooling output. Requirement 2.1.
.kiro/
.cursor/
.claude/
.windsurf/
.continue/
.aider*
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md

# Local addition: planning-only material, not part of the submission.
# Requirement 2.2. Spec documents, steering files and hooks live under
# .kiro/ and are covered by the pattern above.
planning/
notes/
*.plan.md

# Local addition: docs/ is submission material and is tracked, with one exception.
#
# Requirement 2.6 names README.md, docs/CREDITS.md, docs/BUILD-LOG.md and docs/GIT-RULES.md as
# submission material that must be tracked, and the README links to the last three. While docs/
# was ignored wholesale those three links resolved to nothing for anyone who cloned, which made
# the entire technical documentation layer invisible to a marker.
#
# The prompt packs are the exception. They are AI prompts and rubric notes, which is exactly
# the planning and AI-tooling material Requirements 2.1 and 2.2 exclude. They are working material
# for writing the submission, not part of it.
docs/M1-GEMINI-PROMPT-PACK.md
docs/M1-INDIVIDUAL-GDD-AGENT-PROMPT.md

# Local addition: Assets/_Project/ is dead and must never be reported as untracked.
#
# It is the husk left behind when the source folder was renamed to Assets/Project. All code and
# assets live under Assets/Project now; nothing references anything in here.
#
# Leaving it untracked was actively harmful, not just untidy. It holds Models/Group18_Greybox.fbx
# at 304 MB, and .gitattributes routes *.fbx through filter=lfs. The editor's source control
# integration polls `git status --untracked-files=normal` and then calls `git hash-object
# --stdin-paths` on what it finds, and that call runs with the LFS filters live, so every poll
# pushed the whole 304 MB through a temp file in .git/lfs/tmp. That directory reached 96.95 GB
# across 831 files in under an hour on 23 September 2026 and filled a 464 GB disk, which stopped
# Unity from being able to build at all.
#
# Ignoring the path takes it out of the untracked set, so it is never hashed and the loop cannot
# start again. The folder itself should be deleted once someone confirms the 304 MB export is not
# the only copy of anything; Assets/Aside/Art/Blender holds the same greybox at 192 MB, and the
# district has since moved to the Group 15 prefab.
Assets/_Project/

# Local addition: raw shift logs written by PlaytestLogger at runtime. One row per shift, per
# machine, appended forever. The curated record is docs/playtesting/playtest_sessions.csv, which
# a human fills from these; the raw file is a local scratch source, not submission material.
/PlaytestLogs/

# Local addition: git worktrees. These are full second checkouts of the project, Assets and all.
#
# Agents are given a worktree under here so they can edit scripts without making Unity reload the
# domain mid-playtest. A worktree is a complete working copy, so leaving the path untracked puts a
# second copy of every LFS-tracked .fbx into the untracked set.
#
# That is the same shape as the Assets/_Project incident recorded above: the editor's source control
# integration polls `git status --untracked-files=normal`, then runs `git hash-object --stdin-paths`
# over whatever it finds, with the LFS filters live. A worktree in the untracked set would feed it
# the whole Assets tree on every poll. One `git add -A` would also commit the entire duplicate.
#
# Worktrees are disposable by design: `git worktree add` recreates one in seconds, and the branch
# it points at is the durable artefact. Nothing in here belongs in a commit.
/.worktrees/

# Local addition: Hypothesis's example database, written by the property-based tests under
# docs/tooling/repo-checks. It is a per-machine cache of failing examples, regenerated on demand.
.hypothesis/

# Local addition: Python bytecode from the scripts under docs/tooling. Regenerated on every run.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Local addition: editor-local workspace settings. Nothing here is shared with the group, and the
# upstream template only covers Visual Studio's .vs/, not VS Code's .vscode/.
.vscode/

# Local addition: the husk meta file left beside the dead Assets/_Project folder.
#
# Assets/_Project/ is ignored twenty lines above for the disk-filling reason recorded there, but a
# directory pattern does not cover the sibling .meta file Unity wrote for it, so the orphan kept
# surfacing as untracked. Ignoring Unity .meta files is normally wrong; this one is an exception
# because the folder it describes is already ignored and slated for deletion.
Assets/_Project.meta

# Local addition: per-machine measurement scratch files written by the F6 capture in VehicleLab.
#
# The tracked record is VehicleLab_Measurements/vehicle_measurements.csv, which .gitattributes
# routes through merge=union so two people capturing at once do not conflict. Files suffixed
# _local are one person's unmerged working capture, not group data.
VehicleLab_Measurements/*_local.csv

# Local addition: player builds. The upstream template covers /Build/ and /Builds/, but the
# Windows standalone here was written to "Game Build/", which those patterns do not match.
#
# It is 486 MB across 197 files and includes UnityPlayer.dll and the whole _Data folder. Left
# untracked it is the Assets/_Project hazard again: the editor polls `git status`, pipes what it
# finds through `git hash-object` with the LFS filters live, and fills .git/lfs/tmp.
#
# Builds are release artefacts, not source. The record of a build belongs in docs/BUILD-LOG.md
# with its commit SHA, and the binary belongs wherever the group distributes it.
Game Build/
/[Gg]ame [Bb]uild/

# Local addition: shift logs written next to a player build, same reasoning as /PlaytestLogs/.
**/PlaytestLogs/

# Local addition: generated handouts. docs/handouts/ holds .docx and .pdf built from the Markdown
# in docs/ by docs/tooling/md_to_docx.py. They rebuild in one command, so tracking them would mean
# a binary diff every time a source document is edited. The Markdown is the record.
docs/handouts/

# Local addition: scratch scene copies under the agent task folders.
#
# The investigation reports in .agents/tasks/ are kept, because the milestone documents cite them
# as evidence and a dangling citation is worse than no citation. The ref/ subfolders are not: they
# are read-only extractions of scenes that already live in Assets/, pulled out of git so a scene on
# another branch could be measured without checking it out. Hard.unity and Medium.unity alone are
# 11.8 MB of exact duplicate, and .gitattributes does not route .unity through LFS.
.agents/tasks/**/ref/
.agents/tasks/**/tools/
